450
00:30:02,542 --> 00:30:05,875
That old, forgotten case.
Let's recall it now.

451
00:30:11,125 --> 00:30:12,458
Do you remember this girl?

452
00:30:13,667 --> 00:30:14,792
[in unison] Who's this girl?

453
00:30:16,458 --> 00:30:17,625
Who is that girl, sir?

454
00:30:18,083 --> 00:30:22,083
We're here for the Ambrosia Pub case.
Why bring up this girl?

455
00:30:22,250 --> 00:30:24,666
What is the link
between these two cases?

456
00:30:24,667 --> 00:30:26,958
Yeah. Let's find the link.

457
00:30:27,125 --> 00:30:28,750
Please listen patiently.

458
00:30:29,167 --> 00:30:32,750
An accident case that happened
six years ago near Panjagutta,

459
00:30:33,083 --> 00:30:34,750
let's remember that once. Okay?

460
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:39,667
- That master will bore us.
- Let's drink and chill.

461
00:30:40,042 --> 00:30:42,958
It's better to go somewhere
other than the school.

462
00:30:43,125 --> 00:30:45,541
Yeah. That is the reason
we bunked school today.

463
00:30:45,542 --> 00:30:46,500
Dude!

464
00:30:48,208 --> 00:30:49,624
Everyone, take off your uniforms.

465
00:30:49,625 --> 00:30:50,875
- Fast, fast.
- My bag.

466
00:30:51,292 --> 00:30:52,375
Put it on, quick.

467
00:30:53,250 --> 00:30:55,042
Happy hours, dude.
Let's go.

468
00:30:57,792 --> 00:30:58,833
Let's sit over there, sir.

469
00:31:01,375 --> 00:31:04,207
Six B52, two French fries,

470
00:31:04,208 --> 00:31:05,917
- what else?
- Nuggets, dude.

471
00:31:07,417 --> 00:31:08,458
Cheers!

472
00:31:12,500 --> 00:31:16,000
This is the happy hour.
Let's go, dude!

473
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:17,792
Hey...

474
00:31:18,625 --> 00:31:19,875
I have it, dude.

475
00:31:20,375 --> 00:31:21,875
Hey, turn up the music.

476
00:31:35,750 --> 00:31:36,583
Hey!

477
00:31:37,625 --> 00:31:38,500
Are you guys blind?

478
00:31:41,083 --> 00:31:42,332
Aa meena katta meena,

479
00:31:42,333 --> 00:31:44,708
sing a song, ding-a-dong.
carrom board, barrom board.

480
00:31:44,875 --> 00:31:47,500
- S-T-O-P, stop!
- Wow!

481
00:31:49,250 --> 00:31:51,625
- Who taught you this game, dear?
- Friends.

482
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:53,208
I recently met them.

483
00:31:54,333 --> 00:31:56,042
This is too good, dear.

484
00:31:57,500 --> 00:31:58,708
My loved one.

485
00:32:06,042 --> 00:32:08,333
- Hey...
- Mom!

486
00:32:19,208 --> 00:32:20,167
Mom!

487
00:32:26,375 --> 00:32:27,500
Hey, stop!

488
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:43,083
Move aside.

489
00:32:45,250 --> 00:32:46,583
- Hey. Move aside, guys.
- Move aside.

490
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:49,958
We are clearing it, sir.

491
00:32:51,875 --> 00:32:53,417
Brother. Can someone
call an ambulance?

492
00:32:53,542 --> 00:32:55,042
Be careful.
Careful with the girl, brother.

493
00:33:50,208 --> 00:33:51,125
Which hospital?

494
00:33:51,917 --> 00:33:52,875
How's the girl?

495
00:33:53,583 --> 00:33:55,083
How are the brothers?

496
00:33:57,042 --> 00:33:58,167
How's father doing?

497
00:33:58,750 --> 00:33:59,792
How's Renuka?

498
00:34:00,125 --> 00:34:01,042
Is Renuka all right?

499
00:34:02,042 --> 00:34:02,958
Please, drive fast.

500
00:34:19,208 --> 00:34:20,167
Uncle! uncle!

501
00:34:20,500 --> 00:34:22,999
Are there really schools in America?

502
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:25,542
Will kids go to school there
like I do?

503
00:34:25,667 --> 00:34:26,707
Yes, Bhavya.

504
00:34:26,708 --> 00:34:28,624
Once you are done
with your schooling here,

505
00:34:28,625 --> 00:34:31,083
