and passed away.

1528
01:57:26,625 --> 01:57:33,292
♪ Walking ♪
♪ Right beside you ♪

1529
01:57:34,833 --> 01:57:37,666
- ♪ Draw closer ♪
- If I see you involved in this again,

1530
01:57:37,667 --> 01:57:39,542
the entire gang will, okay?

1531
01:57:39,875 --> 01:57:43,417
♪ Relationships ♪

1532
01:57:44,458 --> 01:57:49,125
♪ Did time conceal itself within?

1533
01:57:50,792 --> 01:57:52,875
- Come up.
- Hey Vikas!

1534
01:57:53,042 --> 01:57:54,792
Come, come. Chill!

1535
01:57:54,917 --> 01:57:56,458
Take a shot.

1536
01:57:57,333 --> 01:57:58,666
Come up. Let's go home.

1537
01:57:58,667 --> 01:58:01,042
Home? Where's home?
♪ So many springs ♪

1538
01:58:01,292 --> 01:58:03,042
Ours is a broken home.

1539
01:58:03,792 --> 01:58:06,833
- Oops!
- ♪ So many joys ♪

1540
01:58:08,417 --> 01:58:11,583
♪ So many wonders ♪

1541
01:58:13,042 --> 01:58:16,042
♪ So many opportunities ♪

1542
01:58:17,500 --> 01:58:18,750
Dad!

1543
01:58:28,333 --> 01:58:30,542
Chandramma! Chandramma!

1544
01:58:30,833 --> 01:58:32,583
What happened to
the bottles in my rack?

1545
01:58:33,167 --> 01:58:35,625
Vikas got rid of all the bottles.

1546
01:58:39,542 --> 01:58:42,125
You don't need to punish
yourself for me every day.

1547
01:58:42,417 --> 01:58:44,333
I'll take the exam under your conditions.

1548
01:58:45,083 --> 01:58:46,583
But until then, you mind your business.

1549
01:58:46,875 --> 01:58:47,875
I'll mind mine.

1550
01:58:48,292 --> 01:58:49,250
Otherwise, here...

1551
01:58:51,750 --> 01:58:54,333
The empty shells
from what you fired that day.

1552
01:58:56,667 --> 01:58:58,042
You have to account for them
in the department, right?

1553
01:58:59,833 --> 01:59:02,583
The remaining bullets.
First and second.

1554
01:59:03,250 --> 01:59:05,250
One for you.
Another for me.

1555
01:59:05,458 --> 01:59:07,792
Kill me, and then you kill yourself.

1556
01:59:09,708 --> 01:59:10,667
Otherwise, you tell me.

1557
01:59:11,083 --> 01:59:12,042
I'll kill you

1558
01:59:12,375 --> 01:59:14,375
and live every day dying,
just as you wished.

1559
01:59:18,250 --> 01:59:19,667
But until then, this stays right there.

1560
01:59:33,833 --> 01:59:38,042
[lecturer explains a concept]

1561
01:59:51,542 --> 01:59:54,833
We used ex-prisoners as
fresh peddlers after their release.

1562
01:59:55,125 --> 01:59:57,625
This hampered Sahil's business.

1563
01:59:58,167 --> 02:00:00,958
Vikas and I planned to
take over his business.

1564
02:00:01,792 --> 02:00:04,583
For someone who's facing a life sentence,

1565
02:00:04,833 --> 02:00:06,542
this seemed like the best option.

1566
02:00:06,667 --> 02:00:11,000
That's why Vikas, who was never
interested in parole, came out now.

1567
02:00:12,292 --> 02:00:13,625
Don't delay any longer.

1568
02:00:14,167 --> 02:00:15,958
As part of Operation Euphoria,

1569
02:00:16,500 --> 02:00:18,083
file a petition with the court
to question

1570
02:00:18,250 --> 02:00:20,958
Sahil while he's in our custody.

1571
02:00:21,083 --> 02:00:21,958
Done, sir.

1572
02:00:22,083 --> 02:00:25,333
[lecturer explains a concept]

1573
02:00:37,833 --> 02:00:38,792
What a change!

1574
02:00:42,500 --> 02:00:44,125
- Did you solve it?
- Yes.

1575
02:00:46,000 --> 02:00:49,042
So, y equals
to 9.8 meters per second square.

1576
02:01:02,458 --> 02:01:07,000
Where did you dump the new stock
of drugs you brought in from Goa?

1577
02:01:07,292 --> 02:01:08,250
Sahil...

1578
02:01:09,208 --> 02:01:12,458
I found out you're the primary dealer
in the city's drug trade.

1579
02:01:13,125 --> 02:01:16,042
Your cellmates Amar and
Vikas turned approvers,

1580
02:01:16,333 --> 02:01:18,083
and exposed all your prison activities.

1581
02:01:21,042 --> 02:01:25,875
Your Zumani benami, Bobby
told us everything.

1582
02:01:28,542 --> 02:01:30,332
You could get a second chance, Sahil.

1583
02:01:30,333 --> 02:01:33,416
Hey! You're just an anti-drug officer
in the bureau I run.

1584
02:01:33,417 --> 02:01:34,708
What does that Vikas guy know,

1585
02:01:34,833 --> 02:01:37,083
except for his death, which is
written in my hands?

1586
02:01:37,250 --> 02:01:39,375
If you have the guts, take me outside.

1587
02:01:39,500 --> 02:01:40,917
It's not just about that Vikas guy.

1588
02:01:41,125 --> 02:01:43,333
I'll sort out
the information you need too.

1589
02:01:43,708 --> 02:01:45,875
You should've tasted my stuff!

1590
02:01:46,083 --> 02:01:50,458
If you mess with the guys
who took our mix... they're zombies!

1591
02:01:51,333 --> 02:01:54,208
They'll gnaw away
your department and devour it!

1592
02:02:00,125 --> 02:02:04,167
In jail, all you can do is dream.

1593
02:02:04,458 --> 02:02:05,750
This is your last chance.

1594
02:02:06,125 --> 02:02:09,375
If you don't face reality and
give me the dump details,

1595
02:02:10,292 --> 02:02:13,125
I won't rest until you tell me.

1596
02:02:34,625 --> 02:02:36,375
Vikas, the exam is
tomorrow morning, right?

1597
02:02:36,750 --> 02:02:38,917
Please come home early and
go to bed early.

1598
02:02:39,375 --> 02:02:40,792
Okay, I'm starting.

1599
02:02:44,292 --> 02:02:47,375
Hey, tomorrow morning, I'll come and
drop you off at the exam hall.

1600
02:02:47,958 --> 02:02:49,250
- Okay, Dad.
- Okay. Bye.

1601
02:02:55,667 --> 02:02:57,333
Dheeraj?
Hey...

1602
02:03:00,167 --> 02:03:01,292
How've you been?

1603
02:03:01,958 --> 02:03:03,167
How long has it been
since I saw you, man?

1604
02:03:03,333 --> 02:03:05,375
It's been six years and eighty-two days.

1605
02:03:05,875 --> 02:03:10,958
Our whole lives are getting wasted by
counting years, days, and hours like this.

1606
02:03:12,875 --> 02:03:15,333
Hey, according to you, who
gave evidence against us

1607
02:03:15,792 --> 02:03:17,792
in the Ambrosia case all these days?

1608
02:03:19,042 --> 02:03:20,542
Your mother did all this, man!

1609
02:03:21,458 --> 02:03:23,042
Hey, what are you saying?

1610
02:03:23,917 --> 02:03:26,250
Yes, it's true.
Your mother did all this.

1611
02:03:26,375 --> 02:03:27,708
We got a life sentence
because of your mother.

1612
02:03:45,125 --> 02:03:47,374
Mr. Commissioner, we found the phone
my son destroyed

1613
02:03:47,375 --> 02:03:48,917
in the drainage system.

1614
02:03:49,958 --> 02:03:53,083
- You may find some clues.
- Oh, that's great, ma'am.

1615
02:03:53,500 --> 02:03:56,542
- I'll collect it personally.
- Okay, sir.

1616
02:03:57,167 --> 02:04:00,542
While our parents were trying to
save us from this case,

1617
02:04:00,875 --> 02:04:04,583
your mother got us a
life sentence and ruined our lives.

1618
02:04:08,042 --> 02:04:09,833
There's no chance of this punishment
being reduced anymore, man.

1619
02:04:11,458 --> 02:04:14,000
Other than coming out on parole
like this occasionally.

1620
02:04:15,042 --> 02:04:16,667
That, too, is possible only
when someone shows us mercy.

1621
02:04:20,083 --> 02:04:22,542
My mom is the kind of person who,
saves me just when I'm about to die

1622
02:04:22,833 --> 02:04:25,667
only to make me live a life
that feels like dying every single day.

1623
02:04:26,958 --> 02:04:29,500
But look how you all suffered
because of me, all these days.

1624
02:04:39,250 --> 02:04:40,167
Vikas!

1625
02:04:41,542 --> 02:04:43,250
Where are you off to? Going home?

1626
02:04:44,125 --> 02:04:46,375
Don't forget, the exam is at
9 AM tomorrow.

1627
02:04:47,792 --> 02:04:48,875
Should I come along?

1628
02:05:06,333 --> 02:05:09,625
Hey Vikas! I broke out of prison
just to kill you.

1629
02:05:10,250 --> 02:05:13,667
If destiny wants you alive,
then try getting away from me.

1630
02:05:14,625 --> 02:05:17,125
Perfect. I've been waiting
for death, too.

1631
02:05:17,542 --> 02:05:19,375
Let's see who it comes for today.
You or me. Come on!

1632
02:05:56,125 --> 02:05:57,042
Hello, Aunty?

1633
02:05:57,875 --> 02:05:58,875
Hey, Sahil!

1634
02:05:59,583 --> 02:06:01,166
Surrender yourself. You cannot escape.

1635
02:06:01,167 --> 02:06:03,625
The Task Force police are
also tracking you.

1636
02:06:12,583 --> 02:06:13,542
Move!

1637
02:06:23,083 --> 02:06:24,000
Sir!

1638
02:06:24,542 --> 02:06:25,582
Just as you predicted,

1639
02:06:25,583 --> 02:06:27,832
Sahil, who escaped from jail,
is attacking Vikas.

1640
02:06:27,833 --> 02:06:29,958
- Make sure Vikas is safe.
- Yes, sir.

1641
02:06:30,083 --> 02:06:31,124
He has an exam tomorrow.

1642
02:06:31,125 --> 02:06:33,583
Also, keeping Sahil alive
is important to us.

1643
02:06:33,708 --> 02:06:37,417
We need to stop the drugs he controls
from flooding the city.

1644
02:06:37,583 --> 02:06:38,499
Okay, sir.

1645
02:06:38,500 --> 02:06:42,125
Under all circumstances,
Operation Euphoria must end tonight.

1646
02:06:42,375 --> 02:06:44,208
- I'm leaving right away.
- Done, sir.

1647
02:06:48,750 --> 02:06:52,292
Hey, come at me!

1648
02:06:53,375 --> 02:06:54,333
Hey, Sahil!

1649
02:06:58,417 --> 02:06:59,375
Take right...

1650
02:07:06,750 --> 02:07:07,708
Hey, stop right there!

1651
02:07:12,167 --> 02:07:13,250
Come on!

1652
02:07:15,000 --> 02:07:16,417
Task Force, come in!
Task Force, come in!

1653
02:07:20,125 --> 02:07:22,833
Sir, we've lost sight of Sahil
near Abids. Over.

1654
02:07:23,083 --> 02:07:24,750
Task Force, come in! Sahil's missing.

1655
02:07:25,417 --> 02:07:26,917
Task Force, come in! Sahil's missing.

1656
02:07:39,958 --> 02:07:41,667
Those police officers
should be here any time now.

1657
02:07:41,792 --> 02:07:44,041
All the peddlers will be informed of
when, where,

1658
02:07:44,042 --> 02:07:46,416
and who's supposed to collect the stock
that came from Goa.

1659
02:07:46,417 --> 02:07:47,791
Make sure nothing's left on the system.

1660
02:07:47,792 --> 02:07:49,792
Transfer all the data to a pen drive
and give it to me.

1661
02:07:54,583 --> 02:07:55,542
Hand it over.

1662
02:08:01,958 --> 02:08:05,333
Everyone, leave the state.
North, east, west, south!

1663
02:08:05,500 --> 02:08:07,125
Anywhere! Just go!

1664
02:08:07,667 --> 02:08:08,667
As for me...

1665
02:08:10,958 --> 02:08:12,833
I'll come back with Vikas's head.

1666
02:08:18,417 --> 02:08:19,374
- Akhilesh.
- Sir?

1667
02:08:19,375 --> 02:08:20,833
Switch to that road immediately.

1668
02:08:21,042 --> 02:08:23,708
- I'm also taking the turn. Okay?
- Okay and over, sir.

1669
02:08:30,125 --> 02:08:32,000
Sir, we've located Sahil's hideout.

1670
02:08:32,292 --> 02:08:35,250
He wiped out all the systems,
but we caught two of his men.

1671
02:08:37,083 --> 02:08:38,708
I've got Sahil. I've got him.

1672
02:08:39,250 --> 02:08:41,042
I can spot, I can see him.
I've got him.

1673
02:08:57,667 --> 02:08:58,957
Akhilesh, we've got him.
We want him alive.

1674
02:08:58,958 --> 02:09:00,000
Yes, sir.

1675
02:09:30,500 --> 02:09:31,458
Of course.

1676
02:09:33,667 --> 02:09:34,958
Karma is a b***ch, Akhilesh.

1677
02:09:53,125 --> 02:09:55,125
We need to crack this pen drive

1678
02:09:55,667 --> 02:09:59,250
and take all the drug peddlers
into custody overnight.

1679
02:09:59,833 --> 02:10:00,875
Cease that vehicle.

1680
02:10:06,667 --> 02:10:09,458
Your mom's the reason
why our lives are ruined.

1681
02:10:15,500 --> 02:10:19,333
But you should die every second,
for the mistakes you made.

1682
02:10:19,792 --> 02:10:21,500
My son died long ago.

1683
02:10:22,083 --> 02:10:24,333
Die... Die...

1684
02:10:39,333 --> 02:10:42,417
Sir. Vikas hasn't come home yet.

1685
02:10:43,042 --> 02:10:46,208
- Vivek and I are looking everywhere.
- Don't worry, ma'am.

1686
02:10:46,750 --> 02:10:49,583
We've safely rerouted
Vikas to another road.

1687
02:10:50,125 --> 02:10:53,708
- He should be home any moment now.
- Thank you.

1688
02:10:55,250 --> 02:10:56,833
My son died long ago.

1689
02:10:58,167 --> 02:11:00,958
Die... Die...

1690
02:11:05,250 --> 02:11:07,708
Akhilesh, surround all the targeted areas.

1691
02:11:08,125 --> 02:11:09,542
Heading towards HITEC City, sir.

1692
02:11:11,250 --> 02:11:12,917
We've traced out the entire
west zone of the city, sir.

1693
02:11:15,292 --> 02:11:16,999
We can't afford to miss
even a single dump.

1694
02:11:17,000 --> 02:11:19,000
- Copy, sir.
- Over and out.

1695
02:11:22,208 --> 02:11:23,374
We found large amounts of drugs

1696
02:11:23,375 --> 02:11:25,500
in the lorry yards at
Chaderghat and Chintal Basthi, sir.

1697
02:11:35,458 --> 02:11:36,500
Everything must be destroyed.

1698
02:11:36,667 --> 02:11:38,167
- Leave nothing behind.
- Yes, sir.

1699
02:11:40,292 --> 02:11:41,250
It's done, sir.

1700
02:11:41,917 --> 02:11:42,833
Up in the air.

1701
02:11:44,083 --> 02:11:46,500
If we stay a little longer,
we'll all get high.

1702
02:11:47,167 --> 02:11:48,750
I'm closing down Operation Euphoria.

1703
02:11:49,708 --> 02:11:50,750
Thank you, sir.
Thank you.

1704
02:12:03,167 --> 02:12:04,292
Show me your admit cards.

1705
02:12:13,708 --> 02:12:16,375
Uncle, time's almost up.
We've only got five minutes left.

1706
02:12:18,375 --> 02:12:19,417
Just a second, sir.

1707
02:12:23,125 --> 02:12:24,042
It's over.

1708
02:12:25,292 --> 02:12:26,500
It's all over.

1709
02:12:28,208 --> 02:12:30,708
Even the last chance slipped away.

1710
02:12:32,542 --> 02:12:33,542
Dear God!

1711
02:12:34,458 --> 02:12:36,500
What do you want to do to all of us?

1712
02:12:38,167 --> 02:12:41,250
Is there no way to atone
despite our efforts?

1713
02:12:43,042 --> 02:12:44,125
Can't you forgive us?

1714
02:12:45,833 --> 02:12:47,542
How many more tests will
you put us through?

1715
02:13:00,708 --> 02:13:01,667
Oh, what a pity!

1716
02:13:02,000 --> 02:13:04,750
It would have been good if the boy
could have taken the exam at least.

1717
02:13:05,292 --> 02:13:07,250
She went through hell to
educate her son.

1718
02:13:07,500 --> 02:13:09,333
- But it was all in vain.
- Yes!

1719
02:13:09,708 --> 02:13:11,167
As his mother had always desired,

1720
02:13:11,333 --> 02:13:13,000
he would have gotten another chance.

1721
02:13:41,917 --> 02:13:43,375
Your son is the one
who committed the crime.

1722
02:13:44,417 --> 02:13:46,000
The court has sentenced him for that.

1723
02:13:47,125 --> 02:13:49,208
Wasn't it you
who handed in the evidence?

1724
02:13:50,875 --> 02:13:54,458
I don't understand.
What is your crime in this?

1725
02:13:54,833 --> 02:13:56,500
And what am I supposed to
punish you for?

1726
02:13:56,750 --> 02:13:59,000
A bad root is the cause of a rotten fruit.

1727
02:13:59,500 --> 02:14:01,042
Not just those who committed the crime

1728
02:14:01,542 --> 02:14:04,250
but also those who were
the reason should be punished.

1729
02:14:05,833 --> 02:14:08,167
I am an illiterate parent
who doesn't know

1730
02:14:08,750 --> 02:14:12,167
the basic formula that
'Family is more sacred than the State.'

1731
02:14:14,042 --> 02:14:17,958
It was my negligence and flawed upbringing

1732
02:14:18,500 --> 02:14:19,708
that pushed my son
in the wrong direction.

1733
02:14:21,042 --> 02:14:22,625
He committed a terrible crime,

1734
02:14:23,250 --> 02:14:24,750
one he can never make right.

1735
02:14:25,667 --> 02:14:29,833
He's facing a strict punishment
under the law for what he did.

1736
02:14:30,375 --> 02:14:33,417
The mental pain I've suffered from
all these years isn't enough.

1737
02:14:33,667 --> 02:14:35,250
Even I should be punished, Your Honor.

1738
02:14:35,875 --> 02:14:38,833
A person's morality should be
held accountable by the law.

1739
02:14:39,292 --> 02:14:41,250
Let it begin with my sentence.

1740
02:14:42,917 --> 02:14:43,917
Your Honor!

1741
02:14:45,167 --> 02:14:47,750
Parents like us deserve the punishment.

1742
02:14:50,042 --> 02:14:51,833
I am Vivek Chakravarthy Vemulapalli.

1743
02:14:52,417 --> 02:14:54,833
I'm not just a
life partner of Vindhya Vemulapalli.

1744
02:14:55,500 --> 02:14:57,167
I might not be officially listed,

1745
02:14:57,458 --> 02:14:58,833
but I'm still
a significant part of the case.

1746
02:15:01,458 --> 02:15:05,042
My son threw acid on a girl's face
simply because she rejected his love.

1747
02:15:05,167 --> 02:15:07,958
Had he been raised with the correct
values towards women from childhood,

1748
02:15:08,292 --> 02:15:10,875
the girl's life wouldn't
have been ruined, sir.

1749
02:15:11,292 --> 02:15:14,292
Sir, isn't the trash seen on the road
something that came from our homes?

1750
02:15:15,667 --> 02:15:19,208
I drank every day without
realizing my kids were watching.

1751
02:15:19,792 --> 02:15:21,167
I used to hurt my wife often.

1752
02:15:21,583 --> 02:15:23,417
Now, my son has
surrendered to intoxication.

1753
02:15:23,708 --> 02:15:25,583
Sir, there's no longer
any respect for girls.

1754
02:15:25,792 --> 02:15:27,957
If the cow grazes in the field,
will the calf graze on the bank?

1755
02:15:27,958 --> 02:15:29,375
I deserve punishment too, sir.

1756
02:15:34,333 --> 02:15:37,125
Just as one carefully
nurtures a baby in the womb,

1757
02:15:37,833 --> 02:15:40,750
your kid should also be
raised with the same care.

1758
02:15:41,083 --> 02:15:43,917
This fundamental principle, often
forgotten in the fast-paced culture,

1759
02:15:44,042 --> 02:15:46,667
prompted all parents to reflect.

1760
02:15:47,083 --> 02:15:49,792
Alongside rapidly advancing technology,

1761
02:15:49,958 --> 02:15:52,500
society is racing ahead even faster.

1762
02:15:52,833 --> 02:15:56,667
Our systems are struggling to
keep up or maintain control.

1763
02:15:56,917 --> 02:16:00,333
As people become like machines and
machines become more human,

1764
02:16:00,458 --> 02:16:03,875
we've lost touch with our human values,
and this is what we've all become.

1765
02:16:04,125 --> 02:16:06,958
So we, too, deserve punishment.

1766
02:16:07,250 --> 02:16:10,833
You've already experienced many
punishments that laws couldn't impose.

1767
02:16:11,375 --> 02:16:12,542
And you're still experiencing them.

1768
02:16:12,833 --> 02:16:15,667
You might've neglected your
child in the past,

1769
02:16:15,958 --> 02:16:18,333
